# Local acceptance render output: keep the JSON reports, video and key frames,
# not the full 90-frame PNG sequences. The fault-injection reports are proof
# output of `pnpm gates:faults` and are regenerated by it on demand.
artifacts/local-acceptance/production/
artifacts/local-acceptance/static-camera/
artifacts/local-acceptance/masks/
artifacts/local-acceptance/gates_fault_*.json
# The full-resolution run writes 90 frames of 1080x1920 plus its mask passes.
# The reports and the crops that carry the verdict are committed; the raw frames
# are reproducible from them and would be a couple of hundred megabytes.
artifacts/local-acceptance-1080p/production/
artifacts/local-acceptance-1080p/static-camera/
artifacts/local-acceptance-1080p/masks/
artifacts/local-acceptance-1080p/*.mp4
# Steps 1-8 validation harness: the JSON evidence is the reviewable output and is
# committed. The assembled WAVs are regenerated by `pnpm validate:steps1-8` in about
# a second, and their measurements are recorded in mix/assembly.json.
artifacts/steps-1-8-validation/mix/*.wav
artifacts/steps-1-8-validation/render/

# Blender rewrites these backups on every save; they are pure churn in a diff.
*.blend1
# Next Pip uploads stay local. Manifests and reports in the package may be
# copied out for review; the original binaries are not committed.
theatrical-foundation/proposed/pip-replacement-intake/inbox/**
!theatrical-foundation/proposed/pip-replacement-intake/inbox/README.md
!theatrical-foundation/proposed/pip-replacement-intake/inbox/.gitkeep
# Corrected split-part locations for the pending Pip replacement candidate.
!theatrical-foundation/proposed/pip-replacement-intake/inbox/pip_replacement.glb.part1.bin
